Last year it was;

"Evacuate the house... engage the cinemas... and get this man a ticket!"

This year;

"Some people will wait for the second show... but not us... not us!" 
"First day first show... whatever it takes!"

"Do not go gentle into that good night,
Old age should burn and rave at close of day;
Rage, rage against the dying of the light." - Dr. Brand

“Do not go gentle into that good night,
Old age should burn and rave at close of day;
Rage, rage against the dying of the light.”

"We knew the world would not be the same. Few people laughed, a few people cried, most people were silent. I remembered the line from the Hindu scripture, the Bhagavad-Gita;
Vishnu is trying to persuade the Prince that he should do his duty and to impress him, takes on his multi-armed form and says,  'Now I am become Death, the destroyer of worlds.' I suppose we all thought that, one way or another."

"God save us everyone. Will we burn inside the fires of a thousand suns. For the sins of our hand, the sins of our tongue, the sins of our fathers, the sins of our young."
